Fixes legacy defect L-19: an imported module was included in place, so its SUBs made the rest of the program 'code after a SUB': DIM SHARED there failed with "Statement cannot be placed between SUB/FUNCTIONs" and REDIM SHARED was moved into the top-level runtime SUB ("DIM/REDIM SHARED invalid within a SUB/FUNCTION"), leaving FUNCTIONs with a local array. Modules are now split: declarations before the program, procedures after it (D-25). Expected output is QBasic behaviour.
